    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Make a video explaining how password reset works in our web app: the user says they forgot their password, the app looks up their account, emails them a one-time link, and the user opens it and chooses a new password."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I've drafted the password reset graph. It has four parts: the user, your web app, the user database, and the email service. The email service is outside your app. The flow runs from the user's \"forgot password\" request, to the app's account lookup, to the emailed one-time link, and back to the user, who sets a new password in the app, which saves it to the database.\n\nI assumed the reset link travels inside the email rather than being its own box, and that the new password is saved to the same user database the app looks up. Is the graph right, or should I change anything?",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The graph looks good. I approve it."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Thanks, the graph is approved. Next is the story. Here's what I suggest:\n\n- **Audience:** people who use the app, not its developers.\n- **Takeaway:** a reset link works once, and only for an hour.\n- **Shape:** problem, how it works, outcome. The video opens on the forgotten password, walks through the lookup, the emailed link and the new password, and ends with the user signed in.\n- **Hook:** \"Someone can't remember their password.\"\n\nDoes this suit the video? Tell me if you want a different audience, takeaway or hook, or any notes on what to stress or leave out. Once you approve, I'll save it and draft the script.",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Yes, that story works for me. Go ahead and write the script."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I've drafted the script: one scene, about 56 seconds. It opens on \"Someone forgot their password,\" follows the app's lookup and the emailed one-time link, and ends with the user choosing a new password and signed in. The link's rule (one use, one hour) appears as a callout on the email service. The first line didn't fit its caption, so I shortened it to plainer words.\n\nIs the script right? If you approve it, I'll move on to the title card: \"Password reset, step by step,\" with the description \"Forgot your password? Here is how a reset link gets you back in.\"",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The script looks good. I approve it."
      },
